1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,624
My library book returned itself yesterday. Inside the back cover, a margin note written in my exact handwriting said: page twelve.

2
00:00:09,924 --> 00:00:19,668
I opened page twelve with shaking fingers. A single sentence stared back at me, predicting every word I would speak today.

3
00:00:19,968 --> 00:00:27,912
I tried to defy the book. I stayed silent all afternoon. But the margin note had already predicted my silence.

4
00:00:28,212 --> 00:00:36,252
Panic pulled me back to the library. The old librarian smiled, sliding three more stacks across the wooden desk.

5
00:00:36,552 --> 00:00:46,032
Every single book bore my handwriting. Each volume chronicled the final hours of my life, chapter by terrifying chapter.

6
00:00:46,332 --> 00:00:54,612
Chapter seven described this exact room, the flickering fluorescent light, and the cold metal of the emergency exit.

7
00:00:54,912 --> 00:01:02,664
I grabbed a pen, determined to rewrite the ending. If I crossed out the final chapter, I could break the cycle.

8
00:01:02,964 --> 00:01:11,076
The ink bled through the paper, revealing text underneath that I hadn't written yet, but my hand was moving.

9
00:01:11,376 --> 00:01:18,984
My eyes widened as I realized the cruel truth. I wasn't reading my future. I was authoring my own demise.

10
00:01:19,284 --> 00:01:27,852
The final page was blank, waiting for my final stroke. If every page is already written, who is holding the pen?
